<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Straits Settlements</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1826–1946</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Straits Settlements were a British colony on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strait-of-malacca">Strait of Malacca</a> made up of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/penang">Penang</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malacca">Malacca</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/singapore">Singapore</a>. Formed in 1826 under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a>, they became a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crown-colony">Crown colony</a> in 1867 and were the base of British trade and influence in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malay-peninsula">Malay Peninsula</a>. The colony was dissolved in 1946, when Singapore became a separate colony and Penang and Malacca joined the Malayan Union.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/straits-settlements.jpg" alt="Straits Settlements" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Flag_of_the_British_Straits_Settlements_(1874-1942).svg: Himasaram derivative work: Sderftgyvjkoljoyvgtfrd · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_British_Straits_Settlements_(1925%E2%80%931946).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
